      "notes": "TECHNIQUE DEMO (phase2-design section 5.2): instrument macros. What it exists to prove, in order: (1) VOLUME ENVELOPES WITH LOOP AND RELEASE - every lead phrase ends on '===' (note -2, frames 1-2 rows 28 and 60), which runs vol-lead's tail from its release point instead of cutting, and the intro's `pad` (frame 0 row 0) shows vol-pad's 12-tick swell in, its sustain at 12, and its 9-tick release at row 24; (2) DUTY MACROS - dut-attack on the lead (thin front opening to round on every note), dut-pwm-slow on the pad (a 16-tick timbral sweep, audible because the pad note is 24 rows long), dut-12 on the echo; (3) ARPEGGIO MACROS vs the ARPEGGIO EFFECT, side by side - frame 0 rows 32-63 are arp-bed-maj and arp-bed-min, whose chords come from the INSTRUMENT's arpeggio macro, and frames 3-4 are the same idea as the 0xy EFFECT (param 74 = 04a dominant 7 on the A7, 55 = 037 minor, 71 = 047 major), cancelled with 000 at frames 1, 2, 5, 7 row 0 so nothing leaks into the lead or across the loop seam. ONE-FRAME ECHO: pulse 2's order column is pulse 1's shifted by exactly one frame (order[k][1] is the echo copy of order[k-1][0]), which is the large, deliberate version of the echo trick section 2.2 says to author this way and only this way. Fxx (speed only): F05 at frames 3 and 4 row 0 lifts the B section to 180 BPM, F06 at frame 1 row 0 restores 150 - and because frame 1 IS the loop target, the speed at the seam is restated explicitly rather than inherited. Gxx: a 2-tick snare flam at frame 2 row 27. POLYMETER: the triangle runs a SIX-ROW octave cell (root root octave, one attack every two rows) against 16-row bars in frames 1-2 and 5-6 (tri:1/tri:2), so the octave accent lands on a different beat in each bar and only realigns every three bars; the B section swaps it for an 8th-level TRESILLO bass (attacks at rows 0/6/12 of every bar, tri:3/tri:4). Harmonic colour: A7 as V/ii at frame 3 row 0, spelled by the arp effect rather than by written notes, which is why the accidental count is 0%. The demos are QA fixtures first: the piece is deliberately diatonic so a key-lint regression shows up as a real failure rather than being masked by a chromatic budget. The suite-wide rmsRange convention: the measured two-pass mix RMS +-1.5 dB, declared per song because the design's [-20,-9] window is unreachable on this engine and the floor is -30 dBFS. Measured -21.64 dBFS, declared [-23.14, -20.14]. bpmRange spans 148-182 because the Fxx event is part of the demo."
